void ft_ft(int *nbr);

*******

*nbr itself is a pointer, restores an direction of a variable int.
examples:
int a = 10: there is a box, inside of the box, number 10 is there
&a: the address of the box
int *nbr: there is a paper, written 301
*nbr: with the paper, you walk to room 301, and see the things inside

so:
int a = 10;
ft_ft(&a); // pass the direction of a to the function

So:
void  ft_ft(int *nbr)
{
  *nbr = 42; // *nbr means go the the direction pointing nbr, change the value to 42"
}
